  'admin/ux/updates/guide_intro' => 'The rollback to JavCMS {to} stopped at "{phase}": {why}. Visitors get the maintenance page until runtime/update/maintenance.php is gone. Do the steps below in this order, with the file manager of your hosting or FTP.',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_copy' => 'Put these files back: copy each file on the left over the file on the right (same path; .htaccess and web.config are kept in the backup as htaccess.jcupd.txt and web.config.jcupd.txt).',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_missing' => 'These files have no copy in the backup: put back your own copy, or take the file from the zip of JavCMS {v} (same path):',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_delete' => 'Delete these files (the update added them):',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_dirs' => 'Then delete these folders if they are empty now (the update created them):',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_settings' => 'Settings the upgrade steps changed: copy each file on the left over the file on the right; delete a file listed alone (the upgrade created it).',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_version' => 'In application/extra/version.php the version must be {v} (\'code\' => \'{v}\'); closing the run below writes it.',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_db' => 'The update changed the database: restore the tables {list} from {db} (Admins & backup > Backup & restore lists a whole-database backup; a partial backup has a README.txt).',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_none' => 'No file is left to copy or delete.',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_end' => 'Last: delete runtime/update/maintenance.php, then open Admins & backup > Updates: when every file above is back it closes this run by itself; else tick "I finished the rollback by hand" and press "Close this run" there. With SSH, run php tools/update.php --close-attention instead, while the flag is still there: it deletes the flag itself and clears the web server\'s PHP cache through it.',
  // fix round 5 (up-fix-5)
  'admin/ux/updates/m_attention_closed_rb' => 'Run closed: the rollback was finished by hand, and JavCMS {v} is the installed version.',
  'admin/ux/updates/m_attention_closed_left_rb' => 'Run closed: the rollback was finished by hand, and JavCMS {v} is the installed version, but not every file is as before the update ({n}: {list}): check them.',
  'admin/ux/updates/l_attention_closed_unchecked' => 'The founder closed the run: the rollback was finished by hand; JavCMS {v} is the installed version. Still not as before the update ({n}): {list}; files not checked in time: {unchecked}',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_end_bridge' => 'Last: delete runtime/update/maintenance.php. Then open install.php of this site in the browser where you are signed in to the admin as the founder (it is the update bridge again): tick "I finished the rollback by hand" and press "Close this run" there.',
  'admin/ux/updates/attention_end_bridge' => 'Then delete {flag}. The version the rollback goes back to has no Updates page: close this run here, or afterwards on install.php of this site (the update bridge again) - tick the box and press "Close this run".',
  'admin/ux/updates/attention_flag_gone_bridge' => 'The maintenance flag is gone: visitors get the site again. When every file of the list is back, tick the box below and press "Close this run" (nothing closes this run by itself: the version the rollback goes back to has no Updates page).',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_restart' => 'If pages still behave like the newer version after these steps, restart PHP (or clear OPcache in the hosting panel).',
  'admin/ux/updates/l_close_web_restart' => 'PHP\'s cache on the web server never re-reads files and could not be reset: it may keep the newer release\'s copies of the files put back by hand until PHP restarts. Restart PHP (or clear OPcache in the hosting panel) now.',
  // fix round 6 (up-fix-6)
  'admin/ux/updates/attention_retry_off' => '"Try the rollback again" is off while "I finished the rollback by hand" is ticked: press "Close this run" (Enter in the password field does the same), or untick the box to try the rollback again.',
  'admin/ux/updates/attention_end_db' => 'Then delete {flag}. Once every file is back and the tables are restored, tick the box below and press "Close this run" (the run does not close by itself while the steps name database tables).',
  'admin/ux/updates/attention_flag_gone_db' => 'The maintenance flag is gone: visitors get the site again. Once every file of the list is back and the tables are restored, tick the box below and press "Close this run" (the run does not close by itself while the steps name database tables).',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_end_db' => 'Last, once the tables are restored: delete runtime/update/maintenance.php, then open Admins & backup > Updates, tick "I finished the rollback by hand" and press "Close this run" there (the run does not close by itself while the steps name database tables). With SSH, run php tools/update.php --close-attention instead, while the flag is still there: it deletes the flag itself and clears the web server\'s PHP cache through it.',
  'admin/ux/updates/guide_copy_entries' => 'Then put the entry scripts back: copy each file on the left over the file on the right (a "?" has no copy in the backup: take that file from the zip of JavCMS {v}). From this moment visitors get the site again: JavCMS {v} has no maintenance page.',
  'admin/ux/updates/m_rolled_back_db_failed_kept' => 'The files of JavCMS {v} are back, but the database tables could not be restored ({why}). Restore them from {location}: that backup is kept until {until}.',
);
